<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18112" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφάλλομαι</span></b> , aor.
		inf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφάλασθια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ael.
					<u>VH</u>
					6.14
				</span></i>
			; 
				Ep.
			
			aor.
			part.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπάλμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Bion
					<u>Fr.</u>
					10.15
				</span></i>
			:—<i>spring off</i> or <i>down from,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πήδημα κοῦφον ἐκ νεὼς ἀφήλατο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					305
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ τὴν κεφαλὴν . . ἀφήλατο</span>
			<i>jumped off</i> on to his head, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				147
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφαλόμενος τοῦ ἵππου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Caes.</u>
					27
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
			</span></i> l.c.; of a river, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς πέτρας πλεῖον ἢ στάδιον ἀ. τὴν
					καταφοράν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					10.48.5
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>jump, bound,</i> of a quick pulse, <i><span class="en">
				Ruf.
				<u>Syn.Puls.</u>
				7.5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>rebound, glance off,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπὸ τῶν λείων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>de An.</u>
					420a22
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέτρου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Th.</u>
					906
				</span></i>
			: abs., <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.159
			</span></i>; <i>to be reflected,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῦρ ἀπὸ πυρός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.931b
				</span></i>
			.</div>
